          "text": "WANG Yung-chi 王永吉 (T. 修之, H. 鐵山), d. 1659, Ming-Ch'ing official, was a native of Kao-yu, Kiangsu. He became a chin-shih in 1625, and served as district magistrate at Tat'ien, Fukien and at Jên-ho (Hangchow).",
          "source": "eccp-3674929",
          "kind": "source-wording",
          "status": "imported"
        },
        {
          "text": "王永吉，字修之，江南高郵人。",
          "source": "qsg-volume-238",
          "kind": "biographical-opening",
